Of course, I was still very young at that time, over 17 years of age.

17
00:03:04,440 --> 00:03:06,200
And then to be in the command of a tank,

18
00:03:06,860 --> 00:03:13,280
that really took my entire effort I had to bring in those days.

19
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:17,800
We fought until the almost complete exhaustion.

20
00:03:17,801 --> 00:03:19,620
For three, four days in a row,

21
00:03:19,621 --> 00:03:26,240
You went back only in order to fuel up ammunition, a short sleep, and on you had to go again,

22
00:03:26,380 --> 00:03:29,000
because we had tremendous losses at the time.

23
00:03:32,920 --> 00:03:35,900
It was hot. It was very dusty.

24
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:44,460
This was the fighting on point blank range, because due to the dust and due to the extreme mass of tanks,

25
00:03:44,461 --> 00:03:48,620
we could recognize each other only on the shortest distance and then fire.

26
00:03:49,620 --> 00:03:53,060
They were kind of rough going, I would say.

27
00:03:54,760 --> 00:03:58,820
The failure at Kursk started the long retreat for the panzers.

28
00:04:00,480 --> 00:04:03,980
Germany greatly underestimated the capabilities of their opponents

29
00:04:03,981 --> 00:04:09,060
and overestimated their own ability to maintain the blistering pace of Blitzkrieg.

30
00:04:10,640 --> 00:04:14,700
As the first tanks lumbered across no man's land in World War I,

31
00:04:14,701 --> 00:04:19,900
it must have been hard to foresee lightning war as the future for this new weapon.

32
00:04:21,100 --> 00:04:25,920
These few tanks spread over the battlefield plotted along at a walking pace,

33
00:04:26,180 --> 00:04:30,540
like a bunker on tracks to shield the infantry from machine gun fire.

34
00:04:31,420 --> 00:04:36,460
The lone exception came in November of 1917 at the Battle of Cambrai.

35
00:04:37,380 --> 00:04:42,000
The British massed 400 tanks in the first concentrated armored assault.

36
00:04:44,700 --> 00:04:49,160
The British tank offensive at Cambrai was successful in penetrating the German lines,

37
00:04:49,580 --> 00:04:54,700
but due to the lack of supporting infantry and artillery, the attack eventually petered out.

38
00:04:54,940 --> 00:04:58,540
The Germans were able to reform their lines in front of the British advance.

39
00:04:59,140 --> 00:05:03,900
And this is one of the reasons that the German army did not really consider the tank to be an important weapon.

40
00:05:04,540 --> 00:05:08,440
The German army fielded only one type of tank during the First World War.

41
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:13,960
The ponderous A7V, a 30-ton dinosaur with a crew of 18,

42
00:05:14,460 --> 00:05:19,120
struggled over the countryside at a top speed of less than 5 miles an hour.

43
00:05:19,900 --> 00:05:24,320
By war's end, Germany had built about 20 of these giant tanks.

44
00:05:25,740 --> 00:05:28,220
The Germans, of course, had been defeated.

45
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:29,680
They were demoralized.

46
00:05:30,700 --> 00:05:35,180
The Treaty of Versailles limited them to an army of 100,000 men

47
00:05:35,181 --> 00:05:37,700
with no tanks and no combat aircraft.

48
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:43,080
Germany then was faced with the prospect of having to defend itself with minimal resources.

49
00:05:43,081 --> 00:05:54,500
Their leaders had to come up with a way to mobilize the troops so that fewer men could do the job of a much larger conventional army.

50
00:05:56,480 --> 00:06:01,220
General Heinz Guderian studied British and French theories of armored warfare,

51
00:06:01,820 --> 00:06:08,360
radical new theories that prophesied victory with high-speed tanks and mechanized infantry assaults.

52
00:06:08,440 --> 00:06:10,780
supported by artillery and air power.

53
00:06:12,420 --> 00:06:15,880
While the Allied armies all but ignored the ideas,

54
00:06:16,460 --> 00:06:19,040
Guderian tested and refined these new theories

55
00:06:19,041 --> 00:06:21,220
with an arsenal of dummy wooden tanks

56
00:06:21,221 --> 00:06:24,320
and created the blueprint for Blitzkrieg.

57
00:06:25,400 --> 00:06:28,580
In the beginning of the war, I was under his command.

58
00:06:29,320 --> 00:06:30,840
The general was Guderian.

59
00:06:31,020 --> 00:06:34,780
He was called as the father of the tank units,

60
00:06:35,340 --> 00:06:36,860
of the tank units.

61
00:06:43,591 --> 00:06:54,181
And his idea was to take all the tanks together, followed by armored infantry, followed by artillery, especially self-propelled, and all the other units must have the

62
00:06:54,182 --> 00:06:56,860
same speed in the field as the tank units.

63
00:06:56,861 --> 00:07:02,020
But old-school German leaders viewed Guderian as a renegade.

64
00:07:02,021 --> 00:07:10,780
They firmly held on to the notion that tanks should be dispersed across a battlefront and operate only in support of the infantry.

65
00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:18,820
And Guderian said, no, the tanks must come together and must attack altogether.

66
00:07:19,980 --> 00:07:26,520
In 1933, a demonstration by Guderian and his small tank force settled the argument.

67
00:07:26,860 --> 00:07:32,500
Adolf Hitler, Germany's newly elected chancellor, saw enormous potential and proclaimed,

68
00:07:33,180 --> 00:07:36,740
this is what I want, this is what I will have.

69
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:39,760
And the panzer divisions were born.

70
00:07:45,080 --> 00:07:51,100
German industry secretly geared up to produce the weapons that would put the teeth in the new tactics.

71
00:07:51,101 --> 00:07:58,340
tanks were called truck toron to disguise their identity

72
00:07:58,341 --> 00:08:09,780
the first tank to roll off the assembly line was the panzer kampfwagen one with a crew of two and

73
00:08:09,781 --> 00:08:15,880
two machine guns the tank was simple and inexpensive although armed this first panzer

74
00:08:15,881 --> 00:08:17,480
was intended only for training.

75
00:08:19,540 --> 00:08:25,320
In 1935, the army received the more heavily armed Panzerkraftwagen II.

76
00:08:25,840 --> 00:08:28,100
With a 20-millimeter gun and crew of three,

77
00:08:28,101 --> 00:08:31,800
this panzer gave the army a greater offensive punch.

78
00:08:39,460 --> 00:08:43,940
On April 20, 1938, for Hitler's 50th birthday,

79
00:08:43,941 --> 00:08:48,020
the Panzer divisions proudly displayed their new weapons of war.

80
00:08:52,700 --> 00:08:56,080
We were very proud of having these new tactics,

81
00:08:56,840 --> 00:08:59,700
and we were very proud of having Guderian.

82
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:03,140
We were also proud of having good tanks,

83
00:09:03,460 --> 00:09:07,740
and most of all, we were very proud of being well-trained

84
00:09:07,741 --> 00:09:10,780
for this new kind of armored warfare.

85
00:09:13,940 --> 00:09:15,445
he built it, Suzanne.

86
