00:10:25,740 --> 00:10:27,880
Like a brilliant dress rehearsal,

98
00:10:28,420 --> 00:10:30,820
the campaign in Poland prepared the German army

99
00:10:30,821 --> 00:10:32,860
for the invasion of France.

100
00:10:34,080 --> 00:10:37,080
When the Germans invaded France and the old countries

101
00:10:37,081 --> 00:10:40,520
on May 10, 1940, the Germans had fewer tanks,

102
00:10:40,580 --> 00:10:43,600
about 2,700 compared to more than 3,000 French tanks

103
00:10:43,601 --> 00:10:44,760
and several hundred British tanks.

104
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:48,240
And further, the French tanks were superior in quality,

105
00:10:48,740 --> 00:10:51,700
but they were inappropriately dispersed throughout the country.

106
00:10:51,701 --> 00:10:56,260
Every division, every unit had some tanks assigned to it that were not located en masse.

107
00:10:56,500 --> 00:11:02,560
The Germans, on the other hand, had concentrated their effort in a front less than 200 miles wide at its widest part.

108
00:11:02,660 --> 00:11:04,440
And in there, they had concentrated their armor.

109
00:11:10,720 --> 00:11:16,940
The tactic was a concentrated tactic of concentrating our tanks followed by the infantry.

110
00:11:16,941 --> 00:11:24,720
In the beginning, it was so successful because of the overwhelming force we could master in a surprise attack.

111
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:34,700
In France, we became aware of just how superior our tactics were.

112
00:11:35,260 --> 00:11:43,800
I remember during the attack looking out of my tank and seeing tanks everywhere, in front of me and behind me.

113
00:11:43,801 --> 00:11:48,260
It was this massing that was a reason for our success.

114
00:11:49,120 --> 00:11:55,220
Within 24 hours, we crossed three borders.

115
00:11:55,720 --> 00:12:01,480
We went from Germany to Luxembourg, from Luxembourg to Belgium, from Belgium to France.

116
00:12:02,640 --> 00:12:10,800
And we had the French as opponents, and they were so stunned about our appearance

117
00:12:10,801 --> 00:12:15,420
that they didn't make any resistance whatsoever.

118
00:12:17,120 --> 00:12:19,720
The annihilation of France, like Poland,

119
00:12:20,260 --> 00:12:22,400
was not a victory of superior hardware,

120
00:12:22,980 --> 00:12:24,820
but a victory of superior tactics.

121
00:12:25,940 --> 00:12:29,560
Hitler had pushed his army into war before they were fully equipped.

122
00:12:30,600 --> 00:12:33,500
The attacks were led by the lightly armed training tanks,

123
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:35,520
the Panzer 1s and 2s.

124
00:12:36,180 --> 00:12:38,800
The Germans filled in the strength of the Panzer divisions

125
00:12:38,801 --> 00:12:40,720
