182
00:17:38,841 --> 00:17:43,840
Rommel's daring tactics redefined the concepts of blitzkrieg.

183
00:17:43,841 --> 00:17:48,840
He regarded the tank as the raiding weapon supreme.

184
00:17:48,841 --> 00:17:56,840
He was able to develop tactics that use small groups of tanks and other arms that would penetrate deep into the enemy's rear.

185
00:17:56,841 --> 00:18:00,840
Getting behind the lines, turning up where he was least expected.

186
00:18:00,841 --> 00:18:06,840
And he did this by personal example, leading either with the tanks themselves or flying over them in a light aircraft.

187
00:18:06,841 --> 00:18:09,840
But always up there, pushing, chivying.

188
00:18:09,841 --> 00:18:12,840
Much the same way as Guderian had done in 1939 and 40.

189
00:18:12,841 --> 00:18:16,760
but Rommel carried it to a greater extreme and he wants to be there to keep

190
00:18:16,761 --> 00:18:19,080
behind to keep the momentum going all the time.

191
00:18:19,081 --> 00:18:21,160
He was a raider.

192
00:18:21,161 --> 00:18:28,760
Rommel was our idol for all of us who served in Africa.

193
00:18:28,761 --> 00:18:33,000
But we would have preferred if he wasn't always so far out in front.

194
00:18:33,001 --> 00:18:35,720
We were always worried about his safety.

195
00:18:35,721 --> 00:18:41,480
He would have been on the front.

196
00:18:41,481 --> 00:18:47,640
Rommel the Desert Fox consistently outmaneuvered his adversaries using fewer tanks and men.

197
00:18:48,800 --> 00:18:56,800
Rommel was particularly good at using his tanks as a screening force to draw out the British

198
00:18:57,280 --> 00:19:02,880
into range where he could then fight with what was his major anti-tank weapon,

199
00:19:02,881 --> 00:19:05,520
and that is the dual purpose 88mm gun.

200
00:19:05,521 --> 00:19:12,140
The 88 was in North Africa practically a wonder weapon.

201
00:19:12,320 --> 00:19:16,360
It was able to knock out any Allied tank at a range of 2,000 yards or better.

202
00:19:17,680 --> 00:19:20,660
Operating across the open desert like ships at sea,

203
00:19:21,120 --> 00:19:26,180
Rommel and the Afrika Korps drove the British back into Egypt in less than a month.

204
00:19:26,900 --> 00:19:30,760
Rommel's leadership gave his troops a sense of invincibility,

205
00:19:31,460 --> 00:19:34,040
a feeling that would prove to be short-lived.

206
00:19:34,041 --> 00:19:39,080
In the beginning, I had no fear because I had not felt any pain.

207
00:19:40,080 --> 00:19:42,080
I had not been wounded, not burned.

208
00:19:45,620 --> 00:19:47,360
Fear came a little bit later.

209
