in packing our regiment was three tanks three 34 tanks and our guns was not strong enough

227
00:21:27,721 --> 00:21:40,300
to kill the t-34 so that the first 34 was killed running against another

228
00:21:40,301 --> 00:21:47,660
and the crew commander from our tanks he jumped over and put a hand grenade into the russian tank

229
00:21:48,300 --> 00:21:59,180
It was quite a surprise for us that it could kill us from over 1,000 meters, so we had to find a way to knock it out.

230
00:21:59,620 --> 00:22:06,320
We'd hide behind a hill and wait for it to get really close, and then we'd shoot at it from the side.

231
00:22:06,980 --> 00:22:11,960
It usually took three to four of our tanks to knock out one T-34.

232
00:22:11,961 --> 00:22:12,661
before.

233
00:22:12,662 --> 00:22:20,180
The big disadvantages they had were they had no radio communications and they

234
00:22:20,181 --> 00:22:21,662
have no tank commander.

235
00:22:21,663 --> 00:22:25,720
Their gunner would have to look out the top of the tank, assess

236
00:22:25,721 --> 00:22:30,342
the situation, then duck back down inside the turret to fire.

237
00:22:30,343 --> 00:22:32,160
This gave us time to get

238
00:22:32,161 --> 00:22:36,920
close enough to knock him out.

239
00:22:36,921 --> 00:22:41,920
By late November, the panzers pushed to within 19 miles of Moscow.

240
00:22:41,921 --> 00:22:47,100
But this was destined to be the limit of the German advance.

241
00:22:47,101 --> 00:22:51,980
The invasion force had outrun their supply lines and were soon to face an opponent more

242
00:22:51,981 --> 00:23:00,740
lethal than the high velocity gun of the T-34, the brutal Russian winter.

243
00:23:00,741 --> 00:23:06,680
We had started a two front war and we had made no preparations for this winter.

244
00:23:06,681 --> 00:23:12,940
No preparations for our clothing, for our weapons, or for our engines.

245
00:23:16,700 --> 00:23:19,780
The cold made it incredibly difficult.

246
00:23:20,600 --> 00:23:24,640
It got down to 35 degrees below zero with snowstorms.

247
00:23:25,280 --> 00:23:29,000
We had to keep the engines running all night to keep them from freezing.

248
00:23:29,001 --> 00:23:38,500
There wasn't any heating in the tanks, so the entire inside of the tank would be covered with ice, just from our breath.

249
00:23:38,501 --> 00:23:52,501
All the pipes in our tank froze and we got no fuel, no ammunition, no men.

250
00:23:54,460 --> 00:24:02,100
And the men were without coats and winter clothing.

251
00:24:02,800 --> 00:24:04,080
It was horrible, you know.

252
00:24:04,440 --> 00:24:07,000
There were a few hospitals in the front.

253
00:24:07,001 --> 00:24:13,660
Everybody had the absolute will to stay healthy.

254
00:24:14,660 --> 00:24:22,980
Because if you were wounded, it was more or less a death sentence.

255
00:24:26,100 --> 00:24:31,820
In December, the Russians launched a counteroffensive with troops well prepared for the frigid climate.

256
00:24:31,821 --> 00:24:40,520
on the frozen steps of Russia the panzers endured their first defeat

257
00:24:40,521 --> 00:24:50,320
staggered by the losses the Germans scrambled to regain their superiority

258
00:24:50,321 --> 00:24:55,480
tanks were fitted with thicker armor and the panzer 4 was upgraded with a long

259
00:24:55,481 --> 00:24:57,651
barreled 75 millimeter gun.

260
00:24:57,652 --> 00:25:03,120
In September of 1942, the new Tiger tank was rushed from the factory

261
00:25:03,121 --> 00:25:07,434
to join the beleaguered panzer division on the eastern front.

262
00:25:07,435 --> 00:25:09,980
The Tiger I was originally developed

263
00:25:09,981 --> 00:25:17,480
from the concept of the breakthrough tank to make it so powerful and so well protected

264
00:25:17,481 --> 00:25:21,600
that no allied tank would have a hope of destroying it.

265
00:25:21,601 --> 00:25:25,120
This immense tank was fitted with the deadliest

266
00:25:25,121 --> 00:25:30,757
gun in the world, the infamous 88 millimeter.

267
00:25:30,758 --> 00:25:36,520
With the Panzer III and IV, we could start the

268
00:25:36,521 --> 00:25:40,348
firefight from only about 400 to 1,000 meters.

269
00:25:40,349 --> 00:25:44,260
Now with the 88 millimeter gun and the Tiger I,

270
00:25:44,261 --> 00:25:50,547
we could destroy any enemy from about 1,800 to 2,000 meters.

271
00:25:50,548 --> 00:25:53,900
We could now go into battle with

272
00:25:53,901 --> 00:25:56,740
a great feeling of confidence and superiority.

273
00:26:01,120 --> 00:26:04,600
I remember at the end of 1942 on the northern front,

274
00:26:05,320 --> 00:26:09,180
I was in the Taiga and I was faced with 30 enemy tanks.

275
00:26:10,300 --> 00:26:13,780
I was able to knock out 15 of them without being hit.

276
00:26:13,781 --> 00:26:24,080
There was one big problem.

277
00:26:24,280 --> 00:26:28,360
At 60 tons, we were always in danger of sinking into the mud.

278
00:26:29,500 --> 00:26:33,280
And at the northern front, there was a lot of wet and muddy terrain.

279
00:26:36,500 --> 00:26:40,300
It was hardly possible to find a bridge that we could cross

280
00:26:40,301 --> 00:26:43,400
unless the engineers were to fortify them in advance.

281
00:26:43,780 --> 00:26:50,780
Initially, the Tiger was unreliable and difficult to maintain.

282
00:26:50,781 --> 00:26:55,780
Even after these problems were resolved, German industry could never meet the Panzer Division's

283
00:26:55,781 --> 00:26:58,180
demand for the weapon.

284
00:26:58,181 --> 00:27:04,780
Only 1,350 Tigers were produced.

285
00:27:04,781 --> 00:27:12,320
The fact was, it was never a battle one-on-one.

286
00:27:13,280 --> 00:27:17,160
It was always one against five, one against ten.

287
00:27:18,420 --> 00:27:22,660
It was common for a Tiger to be facing 12 enemy tanks.

288
00:27:23,480 --> 00:27:27,000
I can remember when we were pulling back from Leningrad,

289
00:27:27,001 --> 00:27:29,040
and there were three Tigers.

290
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:32,660
We destroyed 52 Russian tanks,

291
00:27:32,661 --> 00:27:35,980
but they still had more tanks coming at us.

292
00:27:38,940 --> 00:27:43,380
The Russian T-34 was equipped with unusually broad tracks

293
00:27:43,381 --> 00:27:46,660
and was better suited to the harsh Russian winter than the Panzers.

294
00:27:47,320 --> 00:27:48,880
Modern Marvels will return in a moment.

295
00:27:53,740 --> 00:27:56,120
We now return to Modern Marvels.

296
00:27:56,121 --> 00:28:02,940
Hitler had anticipated the Soviet people would crumble under the onslaught.

297
00:28:03,520 --> 00:28:05,720
But their resistance only stiffened.

298
00:28:06,420 --> 00:28:10,420
Hitler launched ill-conceived defenses in Leningrad and Stalingrad.

299
00:28:11,080 --> 00:28:14,720
The armored force was desperately drained of equipment and men.

300
00:28:16,800 --> 00:28:20,720
In the summer of 1943, the Germans regrouped.

301
00:28:22,140 --> 00:28:25,320
Hitler massed his forces for Operation Citadel,

302
00:28:25,321 --> 00:28:30,300
and advanced against a salient that had developed in the Russian lines near Kursk.

303
00:28:31,140 --> 00:28:35,440
Hitler had delayed the attack until his new Panther tank had reached the battlefield.

304
00:28:36,440 --> 00:28:42,200
By contrast with the Tiger, the Panther was a much lighter, much more balanced vehicle.

305
00:28:42,201 --> 00:28:45,360
It was well armoured. It was the German equivalent of the T-34.

306
00:28:45,980 --> 00:28:50,960
In fact, the T-34 in many ways influenced the design concepts that grew into the Panther.

307
00:28:51,520 --> 00:28:54,920
Like the Russian tank, it was designed with sloped armour.

308
00:28:55,320 --> 00:28:57,300
an innovation that better protected the crew.

309
00:28:58,320 --> 00:29:02,140
The firepower of the Panthers' high-velocity 75-millimeter gun

310
00:29:02,141 --> 00:29:04,880
was even more lethal than the Tiger's 88.

311
00:29:05,540 --> 00:29:10,920
From 1943 onwards, it was the one tank that most of the Russian and Allied tank crews really feared,

312
00:29:11,100 --> 00:29:12,380
far more than the Tiger.

313
00:29:14,840 --> 00:29:18,560
The Panther was a real present for us tank soldiers.

314
00:29:18,561 --> 00:29:23,720
It had a much better protection and a much stronger gun.

315
00:29:23,721 --> 00:29:27,840
Now we could engage the enemy at well over 1,000 meters.

316
00:29:30,420 --> 00:29:34,460
With the arrival of the Panther, Hitler was ready for the assault.

317
00:29:35,600 --> 00:29:40,800
However, Russian intelligence discovered the plan, and the Soviets braced for the attack.

318
00:29:41,420 --> 00:29:48,240
With the help of civilians, they dug 3,000 miles of trenches and buried 400,000 landmines.

319
00:29:49,080 --> 00:29:54,400
Along their defensive front, they placed more than 400 artillery guns and mortars per mile.

320
00:29:55,600 --> 00:29:58,620
Guderian pleaded with the Fuhrer to reconsider his plan.

321
00:29:59,320 --> 00:30:02,460
Such an attack would negate all the advantages of Blitzkrieg.

322
00:30:02,960 --> 00:30:05,480
There would be no mobility, no surprise.

323
00:30:05,481 --> 00:30:11,320
The men of the Panzer Corps would not be the highly trained elite force that entered Poland and France.

324
00:30:11,321 --> 00:30:20,200
Later in the war, those who replaced the casualties became younger and younger.

325
00:30:23,340 --> 00:30:29,340
They didn't have any experience, so the old staff sergeants took them aside and said,

326
00:30:29,341 --> 00:30:30,859
Now, my boy, listen.

327
00:30:30,860 --> 00:30:38,380
You follow our advice, we'll tell you what to do, and if you don't listen, you'll be dead tomorrow.

328
00:30:41,320 --> 00:30:43,320
to

329
00:30:45,640 --> 00:30:47,640
July 4th the battle began

330
00:30:47,641 --> 00:30:53,640
2,700 German tanks squaring off against 3,600 Soviet tanks

331
00:30:59,240 --> 00:31:06,760
this was my first battle and the first battle for the punter

332
00:31:06,761 --> 00:31:08,944
It was a murderous fight.

333
00:31:08,945 --> 00:31:14,360
Over one million Russian soldiers and 700,000 German soldiers.

334
00:31:14,800 --> 00:31:20,000
I remember during the battle we thought, now this is the end of the world.

335
00:31:24,080 --> 00:31:29,500
Like the Tiger, the early Panthers experienced numerous mechanical problems.

336
00:31:29,501 --> 00:31:39,380
During the first days it became clear that the engines were not strong enough and could not stand the strain.

337
00:31:40,160 --> 00:31:42,160
And there were problems with the transmission.

338
00:31:43,000 --> 00:31:46,680
The first breakdowns came during our march to the assembly area.

339
00:31:46,681 --> 00:31:53,060
We tried to repair them as quickly as possible and sent them back to the front.

340
00:31:59,500 --> 00:32:04,820
And in the first couple days, it looked like the Germans had some success,

341
00:32:04,920 --> 00:32:08,240
but eventually they simply ground themselves to pieces on the Russian defenses,

342
00:32:08,580 --> 00:32:12,620
and when it was over, the German panzer forces were emasculated.

343
00:32:12,720 --> 00:32:16,480
They were no longer able to conduct warfare as they'd conducted it in the past.

344
00:32:17,680 --> 00:32:22,640
In 50 days of fighting, the Germans lost over 500,000 men

345
00:32:22,641 --> 00:32:25,220
and seven complete panzer divisions.

346
00:32:25,221 --> 00:32:32,220
The panzers were forced into a long retreat and a brutal battle of attrition.

347
00:32:32,221 --> 00:32:41,220
The Luftwaffe had lost air superiority, leaving the tanks easy prey for the Aleutian Sturnovit ground attack aircraft.

348
00:32:41,221 --> 00:32:47,220
For me the worst thing was if we were under air attack.

349
00:32:47,221 --> 00:32:53,220
Now if you are in a tank and they attack you, then you are completely helpless.

350
00:32:53,221 --> 00:32:56,340
We feel like a decoy there.

351
00:32:57,340 --> 00:33:02,640
If the fighter planes are above you and you have nothing to fight them,

352
00:33:03,160 --> 00:33:06,160
and you know it's only a matter of time before they get you,

353
00:33:06,280 --> 00:33:09,080
then the feeling is lousy, so to speak.

354
00:33:10,360 --> 00:33:14,760
The day that Adolf Hitler sent his tanks across the Russian borders,

355
00:33:14,900 --> 00:33:16,400
the day that he lost World War II,

356
00:33:16,860 --> 00:33:20,600
there was no way that the Germans could occupy the Soviet Union.

357
00:33:20,601 --> 00:33:27,500
The fact was that the Soviet Union was a nation of over 140 million people, whereas Germany had only 50 million.

358
00:33:28,240 --> 00:33:30,960
And in a war of attrition, the larger nation was likely to prevail.

359
00:33:32,600 --> 00:33:39,160
In North Africa, the German forces were also feeling the crushing effect of the two-front war.

360
00:33:40,140 --> 00:33:45,860
Fuel and supplies ran perilously short, and air support was virtually non-existent.

361
00:33:46,440 --> 00:33:50,220
When I was there, we had to make the best of everything.

362
00:33:50,600 --> 00:33:57,060
Very, very few tanks, long lines stretched out to be protected by just a few.

363
00:33:57,600 --> 00:33:59,160
We didn't have enough ammunition.

364
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:01,420
We didn't have enough gasoline.

365
00:34:02,220 --> 00:34:05,340
We were also afraid that there was sabotage.

366
00:34:05,341 --> 00:34:15,680
I remember that I put a finger in the jerry can, you know, sniffing whether there was any water mixed in it because we feared sabotage.

367
00:34:15,681 --> 00:34:21,240
I remember sometimes we went into battle and were not gassed up fully.

368
00:34:21,780 --> 00:34:26,160
So we just hoped it would be sufficient, you know.

369
00:34:27,460 --> 00:34:30,940
The Allies had broken the German secret radio codes

370
00:34:30,941 --> 00:34:34,600
so they could intercept and sink supply ships before they reached port.

371
00:34:36,380 --> 00:34:43,120
Rommel was continually forced to scrounge fuel where he could find it,

372
00:34:43,121 --> 00:34:45,680
to use captured equipment.

373
00:34:46,820 --> 00:34:50,980
In May of 1943, when the final German units in Africa surrendered,

374
00:34:51,560 --> 00:34:56,800
almost 85% of their motorized transport consisted of Allied vehicles.

375
00:34:57,900 --> 00:35:02,200
The last tanks the Germans had basically ran out of fuel and had to be destroyed.

376
00:35:03,080 --> 00:35:05,540
The time was over for Blitzkrieg.

377
00:35:05,640 --> 00:35:09,340
Blitzkrieg is something that happened in Poland and in France.

378
00:35:09,341 --> 00:35:15,020
in Africa at the end, there was certainly no Blitzkrieg.

379
00:35:15,740 --> 00:35:20,820
During the Battle of France, the 7th Panzer Division earned the nickname Ghost Division

380
00:35:20,821 --> 00:35:24,700
because no one knew where it was, including the German High Command.

381
00:35:25,380 --> 00:35:27,820
Panzers will return in a moment on Modern Marvels.

382
00:35:31,120 --> 00:35:33,480
We now return to Modern Marvels.

383
00:35:33,481 --> 00:35:42,500
When the Allies invaded Europe in 1944, their main battle tank was the M4 Sherman.

384
00:35:43,920 --> 00:35:49,220
The Sherman was rugged, reliable, highly maneuverable, and simple to maintain.

385
00:35:50,040 --> 00:35:55,920
However, the Sherman was thinly armored, and its gun was incapable of knocking out the German Panther and Tiger.

386
00:35:57,620 --> 00:36:02,540
We could kill the Sherman at a much greater distance than they could kill us.

387
00:36:03,280 --> 00:36:05,640
Their gun was not as powerful as ours,

388
00:36:05,840 --> 00:36:08,120
and it was obvious in a shootout

389
00:36:08,121 --> 00:36:12,460
we could get a lot more of them than they could get of us.

390
00:36:13,020 --> 00:36:16,980
One hit on the Sherman, and it caught fire right away.

391
00:36:18,420 --> 00:36:21,880
We called the Sherman's Ronsons after the firelighter

392
00:36:21,881 --> 00:36:26,880
because mostly with the first round, they blew up.

393
00:36:27,540 --> 00:36:29,780
The Sherman always went up,

394
00:36:29,781 --> 00:36:33,180
shoot in flames for the first round.

395
00:36:34,740 --> 00:36:39,420
The Allies had to devise creative ways to cope with the German technology.

396
00:36:40,260 --> 00:36:42,437
Captured German tanks were shipped to the U.S.

397
00:36:42,438 --> 00:36:44,520
Army's Aberdeen Proving Grounds in Maryland.

398
00:36:46,100 --> 00:36:49,480
German tanks are brought here to Aberdeen and they are tested.

399
00:36:49,960 --> 00:36:51,560
They're tested in a lot of different ways.

400
00:36:52,140 --> 00:36:54,560
They test them automotively.

401
00:36:55,840 --> 00:36:59,020
They drive them across a thing called the wash rack.

402
00:36:59,780 --> 00:37:04,640
They drive them up and down hills to see what kind of grade they can climb.

403
00:37:06,340 --> 00:37:13,100
They drive them up against obstacles to see how much of a vertical clearance they can take.

404
00:37:13,840 --> 00:37:18,720
They fire round after round into them to see where the weak points in the armor are.

405
00:37:19,960 --> 00:37:24,660
And after a while, a picture emerges of just how effective these things are.

406
00:37:25,220 --> 00:37:28,820
And that intelligence information is disseminated to the field.

407
00:37:29,780 --> 00:37:40,480
For instance, the early Panther has the gas tanks located aft, and they are exposed.

408
00:37:40,481 --> 00:37:44,280
And if you know where the gas tanks are, you want to aim for the gas tanks,

409
00:37:44,580 --> 00:37:49,500
because you're not going to penetrate the frontal armor with a 75 gun on the Sherman.

410
00:37:50,140 --> 00:37:55,580
But knowing where the gas tank is, you can aim for that position and kill the tank.

411
00:37:55,581 --> 00:38:00,420
The Germans knew that we were doing this type of testing.

412
00:38:01,300 --> 00:38:03,080
They were doing the same thing to our stuff.

413
00:38:03,400 --> 00:38:06,100
This is a common, everyday practice in war.

414
00:38:07,540 --> 00:38:12,920
In December 1944, the Germans launched their last full-scale panzer offensive

415
00:38:12,921 --> 00:38:14,800
at the Battle of the Bulge.

416
00:38:16,060 --> 00:38:20,080
Now, late in the war, they fought with some of the most innovative weapons

417
00:38:20,081 --> 00:38:21,580
in the history of warfare.

418
00:38:22,520 --> 00:38:25,460
The fight marked the debut of the King Tiger.

419
00:38:25,580 --> 00:38:31,660
tank. The King Tiger was the heaviest tank ever to appear on any battlefield.

420
00:38:31,661 --> 00:38:40,400
It was a real massive brute, 68 odd tons, an 88 millimeter gun, really thick armor.

421
00:38:40,840 --> 00:38:46,340
To most Allied tanks, if a King Tiger appeared on the battlefield, you found an excuse and

422
00:38:46,341 --> 00:38:52,661
left. But they suffered the same tactical drawback as the original Tiger did.

423
00:38:52,662 --> 00:38:53,400
They were

424
00:38:53,401 --> 00:38:57,960
very very slow they were so slow and cumbersome to actually move them even on a battlefield was a

425
00:38:57,961 --> 00:39:04,360
major operation but the germans could never produce their weapons in the quantities necessary

426
00:39:04,361 --> 00:39:11,880
to hold off the allies in germany production of tanks and other heavy military vehicles was

427
00:39:11,881 --> 00:39:15,720
turned over primarily to heavy equipment manufacturers who were used to building heavy

428
00:39:15,721 --> 00:39:23,000
trucks railroad locomotives and dockyard cranes in fairly limited numbers so that they didn't develop

429
00:39:23,400 --> 00:39:26,780
a good idea of the mass production was possible.

430
00:39:27,340 --> 00:39:31,720
In the United States, production of military weapons was turned over primarily

431
00:39:31,721 --> 00:39:38,240
to the major automotive manufacturers who were used to building tens of thousands of vehicles in a short period of time.

432
00:39:39,080 --> 00:39:45,020
The Germans built approximately 5,500 Panther tanks,

433
00:39:45,540 --> 00:39:48,440
and the Americans built 52,000 Germans.

434
00:39:49,320 --> 00:39:51,940
You had two great advantages.

435
00:39:51,941 --> 00:39:59,820
You had the greater number and the greater reliability.

436
00:40:01,160 --> 00:40:07,400
Our tanks broke down every 100 kilometers and couldn't be repaired.

437
00:40:08,120 --> 00:40:14,120
And your tanks, like a clockwork, went on for the whole issue.

438
00:40:15,320 --> 00:40:21,880
The Germans were really overwhelmed by such a volume of equipment.

439
00:40:21,940 --> 00:40:27,560
that it's really hard to fathom how, in many cases,

440
00:40:27,700 --> 00:40:30,640
they held on as long as they did with as little as they had.

441
00:40:31,780 --> 00:40:33,760
Despite the overwhelming odds,

442
00:40:33,880 --> 00:40:38,700
the tank crews never lost the spirit that forged the power of the Panzers.

443
00:40:39,400 --> 00:40:43,500
One of the reasons for the German soldiers' incredible fighting effectiveness

444
00:40:43,501 --> 00:40:46,240
was that even when the chips were down,

445
00:40:47,000 --> 00:40:49,640
he kept fighting long after the point

446
00:40:49,641 --> 00:40:54,780
when perhaps it was even hopeless to continue.

447
00:40:57,120 --> 00:40:59,280
This may be a German characteristic,

448
00:41:00,220 --> 00:41:04,460
but we swore at the beginning of our duty to defend our fatherland.

449
00:41:05,380 --> 00:41:08,980
And that's how we fought, over and over again.

450
00:41:10,760 --> 00:41:13,300
I was wounded four times in the tank.

451
00:41:14,000 --> 00:41:16,600
You can see a souvenir from Egypt in my face.

452
00:41:16,601 --> 00:41:22,720
We as a young soldier, we learn to live inside the tank.

453
00:41:24,000 --> 00:41:32,320
The problem is only if you are in the field and an anti-tank gun hit your tanks.

454
00:41:33,000 --> 00:41:34,320
What happened inside the tank?

455
00:41:34,321 --> 00:41:35,840
What happened inside the tank?

456
00:41:37,360 --> 00:41:40,960
It starts a big fire inside the tank.

457
00:41:42,600 --> 00:41:44,560
A lot of dust inside the tank.

458
00:41:44,561 --> 00:41:50,960
and later it's absolutely quiet and you will ask the crew

459
00:41:50,961 --> 00:41:54,600
William are you living? Charles are you living?

460
00:41:55,880 --> 00:41:59,760
and so on. I lost the tank

461
00:41:59,761 --> 00:42:01,400
in five times

462
00:42:01,401 --> 00:42:07,620
and I lost one soldier who was died in the same time

463
00:42:07,621 --> 00:42:12,100
all the others are only wounded. Myself lost one eye

464
00:42:12,101 --> 00:42:16,820
And all the others go in my head because the crew commander looks up at the tank.

465
00:42:17,640 --> 00:42:18,340
With his head.

466
00:42:21,620 --> 00:42:25,220
We were young and didn't think much about danger.

467
00:42:25,880 --> 00:42:31,540
But the worst would certainly have been if the tank caught fire and we couldn't get out.

468
00:42:32,920 --> 00:42:35,480
The crew was very dependent on each other.

469
00:42:36,700 --> 00:42:40,280
If there was a hit on the tank, it affected all of us.

470
00:42:42,100 --> 00:42:43,520
Anything else you would like to add?

471
00:42:44,100 --> 00:42:45,560
Möchten Sie noch etwas hinzufügen?

472
00:42:47,840 --> 00:42:49,700
Wir haben so viel Schreckliches erlebt.

473
00:42:51,500 --> 00:42:53,480
Es darf keinen Krieg wieder gehen.

474
00:42:54,140 --> 00:42:57,560
We have experienced so many terrible things.

475
00:42:58,700 --> 00:43:00,880
There should never be a war again.

476
00:43:05,140 --> 00:43:07,700
Would you believe that the Romans had...

